 ## Background
-The Marching Cubes algorithm was introduced by William E. Lorensen and Harvey E. Cline in 1987 [S1, S7, unofficial]. The lookup table approach was developed to optimize the algorithm by precomputing the 256 possible triangulation cases, eliminating the need for runtime decision trees. The standard table handles ambiguous cases by fixing a specific triangulation, though later work (e.g., [S4, unofficial][S13]) proposed methods to resolve ambiguities using inverse configurations or sub-block subdivision. The method is widely used in real-time graphics and scientific visualization [S7, unofficial].
